name><surname>Barthold</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Coleman</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhatt</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name><name><surname>Osbaldiston</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Jonas</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The etiology of transmissible murine colonic hyperplasia</article-title><source>Lab Anim Sci</source><year>1976</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>889</fpage><lpage>894</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1018473</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b5"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berger</surname><given-names>CN</given-names></name><name><surname>Crepin</surname><given-names>VF</given-names></name><name><surname>Jepson</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Arbeloa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Frankel</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The mechanisms used by enteropathogenic E. coli to control filopodia dynamics</article-title><source>Cell Microbiol</source><comment>in press. doi: <ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1111/j.1462-5822.2008.01254.x">10.1111/j.1462-5822.2008.01254.x</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="b6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beuzon</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Meresse</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Unsworth</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruiz-Albert</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Garvis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Waterman</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title><italic>Salmonella</italic> maintains the integrity of its intracellular vacuole through the action of SifA</article-t